    &= \sigma(\beta \log \frac{\pi^*(y_2|x)}{\pi_\mathrm{ref}(y_2|x)} - \beta \log \frac{\pi^*(y_1|x)}{\pi_\mathrm{ref}(y_1|x)}  - \alpha (A_\theta(x, y_2) -  A_\theta(x, y_1)))
\end{align}

Since the advantage contains a $V_\theta(x)$ term that cancels similarly to the partition function $Z(x)$:

Since the advantage contains a $V_\theta(x)$ term that cancels similarly to the partition function $Z(x)$:

